# Product
UX
1. Enter voice chat
2. Give it a prompt 
    1. What’s the weather in London?
3. Wait for UI to generate
    1. This might take a while, maybe 10 seconds or more
4. Component pops up in movable space
    1. Backend will know which space is available in the movable space

Features
- Components are draggable and can be laid out flexibly in whichever layout the user prefers
- Components can be read-only or require interaction
- If the components require interaction, they will use an MCP server
- To start, we will just set up a timer that counts down to a specific time.

Concerns
- Browser permissions required for certain components (timer → notification)
- Account setup required for some components (Calendar events → Google OAuth)

Interaction
- When backend generates a component, the position of the component should be specified
- The frontend should indicate to the backend what the next grid position available is and/or how much grid space is available
- When the user changes the position or size of the component, the backend should be notified so that state is stored.
